# Pillar / reconciliation / fusion invariants

Full detail: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §7 (decisions D1–D5) and `AGENTS.md` §5.

- `unavailable` pillar emissions are `Ok`, never `Err`.
- `structural` absence → excluded from the D2 mask (`false`); `transient`
  absence → stays in the mask, D4 age-inflation handles it.
- `R^(p)(Δ)` must use D4's bounded saturating exponential — never a linear or
  unbounded form.
- `Ω_t` (RMT rotation) is computed only on common support
  (`members(t) ∩ members(t−Δ)`), both eigenvectors renormalized first — never
  across a rebalance date on full 500-dim vectors.
- `AR_t` belongs in `seraph/features/cross_sectional.py` (C4), never inside
  `seraph/pillars/rmt/` (C6).
- `seraph/fusion/score.py` (C9) is a pure function — no DB calls, no import of
  `seraph/validation/` (C10).
